msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"transpilation-explanation\" />\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Transpile bosonic circuits {#transpile-bosonic-circuits}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This guide explains how to transpile a "
"[`BosonicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-"
"bosonic-circuit#qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit "
"\"qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit\") to a standard "
"[`QuantumCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit)."
" A bosonic circuit carries no truncation, no encoding, and no qubit count "
"(see [Work with bosonic circuits](circuit#bosonic-circuit-explanation)), so "
"the transpiler is where those choices are made. The truncation and the "
"encoding are described by a "
"[`LevelSpec`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-level-"
"spec#qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec\") "
"(see [Describe the truncation with a LevelSpec](mappers#level-spec-"
"explanation)), and the mapper that turns operators into qubit operators is "
"described in [Map operator representations](mappers#mappers-explanation). "
"The result is an ordinary "
"[`QuantumCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit),"
" so any Qiskit-compatible simulator can run it.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The guide uses one small example throughout: two bosonic modes, a state with"
" one boson in each, and a single time evolution under a Bose-Hubbard "
"Hamiltonian whose bond and on-site terms are in separate groups (see [Group "
"operator terms: use the operator structure](grouping#grouping-"
"explanation)):\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Transpilation stages {#transpilation-stages}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As explained in "
"[`qiskit_bosons.transpiler`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-"
"bosons/transpiler#module-qiskit_bosons.transpiler "
"\"qiskit_bosons.transpiler\"), the preset pass managers in this package "
"split the transpilation into the following stages:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Input** {#input}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Converts the circuit to a directed acyclic graph (DAG) data structure, the "
"representation that every later pass works on.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Optimization** {#optimization}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Keeps the circuit in bosonic space. These passes use the structure of the "
"bosonic operators, in particular their groups, while no qubit information "
"exists yet. [`B2BSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-"
"bosons/transpiler-"
"passes-b-2-b-synthesis#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.B2BSynthesis "
"\"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.B2BSynthesis\") is the pass that breaks "
"gates down here, with a plugin for each type of gate: a product formula or "
"qDRIFT for an [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-"
"bosons/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution "
"\"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution\"), and the Clements mesh for a "
"[`ModeRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-"
"library-mode-rotation#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.ModeRotation "
"\"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.ModeRotation\") (see [Synthesize an "
"Evolution gate in bosonic space](bosonic-synthesis#bosonic-synthesis-"
"explanation) for how a method is chosen). "
"[`RelabelModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-"
"passes-relabel-modes#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.RelabelModes "
"\"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.RelabelModes\") reorders the modes. The "
"preset decomposes mode rotations in this stage and leaves everything else as"
" it is.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Layout** {#layout}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Maps each bosonic mode register to a quantum register. A bosonic mode "
"generally occupies several qubits ($d$ of them under the unary encodings, "
"$\\lceil \\log_2 d \\rceil$ under the compact ones), so the quantum register"
" is wider than the mode register. "
"[`OccupationB2QLayout`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-"
"bosons/transpiler-passes-"
"occupation-b-2-q-layout#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.OccupationB2QLayout "
"\"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.OccupationB2QLayout\") derives the "
"register width from a [`LevelSpec`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-"
"bosons/mappers-level-spec#qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec "
"\"qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec\").\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Synthesis** {#synthesis}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Converts bosonic gates to qubit operations, one plugin per gate type. "
"Encoding happens in this step: the plugin for an "
"[`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-"
"library-evolution#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution "
"\"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate maps its operator to a "
"qubit operator, and the plugin for an "
"[`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-"
"library-initialize-modes#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.InitializeModes "
"\"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") gate sets the qubits that"
" encode each occupation. A barrier is carried onto every qubit of each "
"register it touched.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Qubit** {#qubit}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Transpiles the resulting qubit circuit with Qiskit’s own methods, for "
"example to a basis gate set or a device. The preset always includes it; by "
"default it is Qiskit’s preset pass manager, which synthesizes every "
"evolution into gates (see [Continue on the qubit level](#transpilation-"
"qubit-stage)).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Output** {#output}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Converts the internal DAG data structure back to a "
"[`QuantumCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The truncation and the encoding are not stored in the circuit. They are "
"given to the transpiler, and the layout, the state preparation, and the "
"mapper must all agree on them. The preset ensures that by handing the same "
"[`LevelSpec`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-level-"
"spec#qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec\") to"
" all three.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "A practical example {#a-practical-example}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[`generate_preset_occupation_pass_manager()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-"
"bosons/transpiler-presets-generate-preset-occupation-pass-"
"manager#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.presets.generate_preset_occupation_pass_manager"
" "
"\"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.presets.generate_preset_occupation_pass_manager\")"
" builds the pipeline from a spec. Lowering the example under two encodings "
"only changes the spec. The preset ends in Qiskit’s own qubit-level "
"transpilation, which would synthesize the evolution into gates. To see the "
"circuit exactly as the bosonic stages emit it, empty that stage first:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The two encodings use six and four qubits respectively (three levels per "
"mode under the unary encoding, two qubits per mode under the Gray code), but"
" the structure of the circuit is the same: two "
"[`XGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.XGate)"
" operations prepare the occupations, and one "
"[`PauliEvolutionGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.PauliEvolutionGate)"
" carries the evolution.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Compare with the traditional workflow {#compare-with-the-traditional-"
"workflow}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The [bosonic circuits](circuit#bosonic-circuit-explanation) guide describes "
"the traditional workflow, which maps the Hamiltonian to a qubit operator "
"*before* it builds the "
"[`QuantumCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit)."
" The two routes produce equivalent circuits. They differ in what has to be "
"redone when the truncation changes. The bosonic circuit is built once and "
"lowered at every cutoff, whereas the map-first route needs the operator "
"mapped again and the circuit rebuilt:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The entangling-gate count depends on how Qiskit synthesizes the evolution "
"gate, which changes between releases, so plot it:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![CX count of the lowered circuit against the number of levels d, growing "
"quickly with d.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-bosons/transpilation-4.avif)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The count grows quickly with the cutoff, which is the reason to keep the "
"cutoff a parameter of the transpilation and not of the circuit. The two "
"routes are equivalent here, but only the bosonic one can also interleave the"
" grouping of the operator with the product formula (see [Synthesize an "
"Evolution gate in bosonic space](bosonic-synthesis#bosonic-synthesis-"
"explanation)) or hand the encoding to a different spec without changing a "
"line of the circuit.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A spec with a single cutoff leaves the number of modes open, so one pass "
"manager serves circuits of any width. A spec with one cutoff per mode fixes "
"the width:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Build the pipeline by hand {#build-the-pipeline-by-hand}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The preset is a "
"[`MultiStagePassManager`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.passmanager.MultiStagePassManager)"
" with one entry per stage. You can assemble the same pipeline from its "
"parts, which is the starting point for every customization below:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The mapper function receives an operator and the width of the register that "
"the layout derived, and returns a "
"[`SparseObservable`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.SparseObservable)."
" Because it is given the width, passing `num_qubits` on to "
"[`occupation_encoding()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-"
"bosons/mappers-library-occupation-"
"encoding#qiskit_bosons.mappers.library.occupation_encoding "
"\"qiskit_bosons.mappers.library.occupation_encoding\") makes the mapper "
"check that the spec fits the register, so a mismatch between the layout and "
"the encoding fails with a clear message.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Advanced workflows {#advanced-workflows}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Provide an explicit layout {#provide-an-explicit-layout}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[`CustomB2QLayout`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-"
"bosons/transpiler-passes-"
"custom-b-2-q-layout#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.CustomB2QLayout "
"\"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.CustomB2QLayout\") replaces the layout "
"stage with a mapping that you provide, from each bosonic register of the "
"circuit to a quantum register. It is useful when the register must be wider "
"than the spec needs, for example to leave idle qubits for other purposes:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Warning\" type=\"caution\">\n"
"  A custom layout is your responsibility. The synthesis plugins still address qubits through the spec, so a register that does not match the spec’s widths gives a wrong circuit or an error deep inside a plugin. A custom layout also skips the check that [`OccupationB2QLayout`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-occupation-b-2-q-layout#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.OccupationB2QLayout \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.OccupationB2QLayout\") performs after [`RelabelModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-relabel-modes#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.RelabelModes \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.RelabelModes\") (see the next section).\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Reorder the modes {#reorder-the-modes}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[`RelabelModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-"
"passes-relabel-modes#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.RelabelModes "
"\"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.RelabelModes\") is an optimization-stage "
"pass that reorders the modes. The permutation is read as a mapping from "
"original to new mode index, and it is recorded in the circuit metadata. The "
"reordering changes which qubits each mode occupies, and so it can reduce the"
" depth of the lowered circuit.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Because the result is expressed in the new mode order, measured bitstrings "
"must be mapped back before they are interpreted. With several qubits per "
"mode, the mapping acts on blocks of qubits and not on single bits. The "
"following example relabels three modes, each occupying two qubits under the "
"Gray code, and recovers the original occupation from the measured counts:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The restored bitstring is what the circuit produces without the relabeling, "
"read in Qiskit’s little-endian order: mode 0 holds the Gray code of level "
"two (`11`), mode 1 holds level zero (`00`), and mode 2 holds level one "
"(`01`).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<DoqAdmonition type=\"caution\" title=\"Warning\">\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  A spec that gives the modes **different** cutoffs cannot be combined with "
"[`RelabelModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-"
"passes-relabel-modes#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.RelabelModes "
"\"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.RelabelModes\"). The cutoffs are attached "
"to the modes by their position, so reordering the modes would put a cutoff "
"on the wrong mode. "
"[`OccupationB2QLayout`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-"
"bosons/transpiler-passes-"
"occupation-b-2-q-layout#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.OccupationB2QLayout "
"\"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.OccupationB2QLayout\") refuses a relabeled"
" circuit in that case:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "</DoqAdmonition>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Choose the synthesis plugins {#choose-the-synthesis-plugins}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[`B2QSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-"
"passes-b-2-q-synthesis#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.B2QSynthesis "
"\"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.B2QSynthesis\") has no default plugins; "
"the preset registers one per gate type. The available plugins are managed by"
" [`B2QSynthesisPluginManager`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-"
"bosons/transpiler-passes-synthesis-b-2-q-synthesis-plugin-"
"manager#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.synthesis.B2QSynthesisPluginManager "
"\"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.synthesis.B2QSynthesisPluginManager\"), "
"which lists them by the name of the gate they act on:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The two builtin methods are `Evolution.MapperFn` and "
"`InitializeModes.Occupation`. The first synthesizes an evolution from any "
"mapper function, which is how a custom encoding is plugged in (see [Map "
"operator representations](mappers#mappers-explanation)). The library ships "
"no plugin for a [`ModeRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-"
"bosons/circuit-library-mode-"
"rotation#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.ModeRotation "
"\"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.ModeRotation\") gate. The preset breaks it "
"down in bosonic space into "
"[`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-"
"library-evolution#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution "
"\"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution\") gates first, which the first "
"method then handles, but a plugin registered for `ModeRotation` can lower "
"the gate directly instead; see [Rotate bosonic modes](mode-rotation#mode-"
"rotation-explanation) and [Lower a rotation without decomposing it](mode-"
"rotation#mode-rotation-direct-explanation). You can register a method by "
"name through the `config` argument of "
"[`B2QSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-"
"passes-b-2-q-synthesis#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.B2QSynthesis "
"\"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.B2QSynthesis\"), or write a plugin object "
"into [`B2QSynthesis.methods`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-"
"bosons/transpiler-"
"passes-b-2-q-synthesis#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.B2QSynthesis.methods "
"\"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.B2QSynthesis.methods\") directly, as the "
"preceding examples do.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"transpilation-qubit-stage\" />\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Continue on the qubit level {#continue-on-the-qubit-level}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The preset always ends in a `qubit` stage, which is Qiskit’s own preset pass"
" manager. Keyword arguments of "
"[`generate_preset_occupation_pass_manager()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-"
"bosons/transpiler-presets-generate-preset-occupation-pass-"
"manager#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.presets.generate_preset_occupation_pass_manager"
" "
"\"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.presets.generate_preset_occupation_pass_manager\")"
" are handed to "
"[`qiskit.transpiler.generate_preset_pass_manager()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.generate_preset_pass_manager),"
" so you can translate to a basis gate set or target a device directly. "
"Prefer `optimization_level=0` to keep the circuit close to what the bosonic "
"stages produced:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Two other choices are common. Assign an empty "
"[`PassManager`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.PassManager)"
" to the `qubit` stage when you want to show the circuit exactly as the "
"pipeline synthesized it, as the examples above do. Or assemble the pipeline "
"yourself and add any Qiskit pass manager as the `qubit` stage of the "
"[`MultiStagePassManager`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.passmanager.MultiStagePassManager)."
" Stages run in the order they are given, so the `qubit` stage must come "
"before `output`, because Qiskit’s passes expect a DAG and not a finished "
"circuit:\n"
msgstr ""

